From: Saravana Kannan <saravanak@google.com>
Subject: [PATCH] driver core: fw_devlink: Make the error message a bit more useful

Diagnostic backport of the upstream message change. This changes neither
link construction nor error severity. It identifies the firmware consumer
behind proxy links so that missing child-device associations can be fixed.

Source: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20241024061347.1771063-4-saravanak@google.com/

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://lore.kernel.org/all/20241024061347.1771063-4-saravanak@google.com/]

Signed-off-by: Saravana Kannan <saravanak@google.com>
---
 drivers/base/core.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/base/core.c b/drivers/base/core.c
--- a/drivers/base/core.c
+++ b/drivers/base/core.c
@@ -2237,9 +2237,9 @@ static int fw_devlink_create_devlink(struct device *con,
 		}

 		if (con != sup_dev && !device_link_add(con, sup_dev, flags)) {
-			dev_err(con, "Failed to create device link (0x%x) with %s\n",
-				flags, dev_name(sup_dev));
+			dev_err(con, "Failed to create device link (0x%x) with supplier %s for %pfwf\n",
+				flags, dev_name(sup_dev), link->consumer);
 			ret = -EINVAL;
 		}

 		goto out;
